--- A moment's text reads back as the moment, in every year a moment holds:
--- outside 0 to 9999 the year is written with its sign and four digits or
--- more, as ISO 8601's expanded form and `fmt`'s date style write it. The
--- sign had counted among the four digits (`-005-06-01`), which read back a
--- day off, and a year past 9999 had not read back at all (Rosetta Code,
--- Find the last Sunday of each month).

for y in [-5, 0, 1, 1969, 9999, 10000, 200000]
    t = moment[y, 6, 1]
    back = moment[str[t]]
    log[str[t], fmt[t, style = 'date'], back eq t, moment[fmt[t, style = 'date']] eq t]
u = moment[-44, 3, 15, 12, 30, 0]
log[u, moment[str[u]] eq u]
log[encode[[moment[12345, 1, 2]]]]
